.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man1/showkey.1, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt SHOWKEY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm showkey
.Nd print keyboard scan codes, keycodes or translated bytes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a | k | s
.Op Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the keys read from the kernel console.
Run it there with no other keyboard reader.
It cannot examine the keyboard through a terminal emulator's pseudo-terminal.
In keycode or scan-code mode it exits after ten seconds without a key event,
or on a termination signal, and restores the keyboard's previous mode.
In translated mode Control-D ends input.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Print translated bytes in decimal, octal and hexadecimal.
.It Fl k
Print keycodes and whether each key was pressed or released.
This is the default.
.It Fl s
Print scan-code bytes in hexadecimal.
.It Fl h
Print help.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dumpkeys 1 ,
.Xr kbd_mode 1 ,
.Xr loadkeys 1
